  "pitch_paragraph": "The tightest structure in the bank and the shortest runtime — 2:25, hook in your hands by 0:24, and three choruses that each arrive out of a hard cut to near silence. That drop is the record's signature move: it pulls the floor out for a bar and lets the chorus land in the space, and it works all three times. The topline is built for a group — it spends most of its time between A3 and A4, low enough to hand around comfortably, then opens all the way to G5 when it wants a moment, so there's a natural low part and a real ceiling for a main vocal. It sways rather than pushes at 86, bright up top with the bridge at 1:30 clearing out completely — the obvious slot for a dance break.",
